title: Authorizations › New Case › Clinical documentation › Required and typical documents by type
route: /authorizations/new/:draftId (step 3 of 5, the Documents list)
intro: Which documents a case needs comes from two places. The required ones come from the payer's saved list for the level of care (Payers › Rules & Instructions › Clinical documentation). What a request of this type usually carries is added under them and labelled 'Typical for a continued stay' and so on. Typical items are the demo's advice, never a payer's rule, and never required. 'N of M ready' counts both.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Open Clinical documentation\nThe Authorization type decides the typical items"
process pReq "Required documents\nThe list saved on Payers › Rules & Instructions › Clinical documentation for this payer and level of care\nSummit Residential 3.5: 9 documents, 7 required\nNo payer or level of care yet: only the referral and the diagnosis report"
goto gPayers "Continues in: Payers › Rules & Instructions › Edit the document list"
decision dKind "Which Authorization type?"
process t1 "Initial authorization\nNo extra typical items\nThe payer's list is the list"
process t2 "Concurrent review · 'Typical for a continued stay'\nProgress note since the last review\nUpdated treatment plan\nCurrent ASAM reassessment\nStep-down or discharge plan"
process t3 "Reauthorization / renewal · 'Typical for a renewal'\nProgress summary since the last authorization\nUpdated treatment plan\nCurrent ASAM reassessment\nAttendance record"
process t4 "Modification / extension · 'Typical for a modification'\nClinical note that supports the change\nUpdated treatment plan\nThe current authorization letter"
process t5 "Retroactive authorization · 'Typical for a retroactive authorization'\nAdmission order with its date\nEligibility check from the admission date\nAttendance record for the dates of service\nWhy the authorization was not obtained"
decision dFit "Does the title fit a standard document the payer already lists?\ne.g. 'Updated treatment plan' fits Treatment plan, 'Current ASAM reassessment' fits ASAM assessment"
process pSame "It is not listed twice\nA dropped file fills the one row"
process pOwn "It is its own row\nReader cannot match a file by name, so the person adds it"
screen sRow "The Documents list\nRequired first · Recommended · Typical for the type · 'Not on the list' for a file the payer does not ask for"
process pHint "A typical row says 'Typical for a continued stay. You can continue without it.'\nA required row says 'Not found yet. Drop it above or add it here.'"
process pCount "Progress line 'N of M ready'\nRequired plus typical, with 'Mark not available' counting as ready\n'3 of 4 ready' reads three items in and one to go"
process pJust "Authorization preparation lists a missing typical item as evidence that is missing\n'... is not in the case. It is typical for a continued stay.'"
goto gRows "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Clinical documentation › Clinical summary and document rows"
goto gMark "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Clinical documentation › Replace a document or mark it not available"
goto gJust "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Authorization preparation › Justification by type"
goto gRev "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Review & submit › Validation summary and checks"

s1 --> pReq --> dKind
pReq -.-> gPayers
dKind -->|Initial| t1
dKind -->|Concurrent| t2
dKind -->|Reauthorization| t3
dKind -->|Modification| t4
dKind -->|Retroactive| t5
t2 --> dFit
t3 --> dFit
t4 --> dFit
t5 --> dFit
t1 --> sRow
dFit -->|Yes| pSame --> sRow
dFit -->|No| pOwn --> sRow
sRow --> pHint --> pCount
pCount --> pJust --> gJust
sRow --> gRows
sRow --> gMark
pCount -.-> gRev
